est"},{"type":"h","text":"Aerodynamics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lift/drag"},{"text":"Boundary layers"},{"text":"Airfoil theory"},{"text":"Compressible flow"},{"text":"Shock waves"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Propulsion"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brayton cycle"},{"text":"Turbomachinery"},{"text":"Nozzle flow"},{"text":"Thrust"},{"text":"Specific impulse"},{"text":"Combustion"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Structures"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stress/strain"},{"text":"Bending"},{"text":"Torsion"},{"text":"Fatigue"},{"text":"Buckling"},{"text":"Composite materials"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Flight dynamics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stability"},{"text":"Aircraft equations of motion"},{"text":"Control surfaces"},{"text":"Longitudinal/lateral dynamics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"GNC"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PID"},{"text":"State-space"},{"text":"Kalman filter"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Sensor fusion"},{"text":"Trajectory planning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Differential equations"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Numerical methods"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For an R&D career, postgraduate study can significantly deepen specialisation, although the exact requirement depends on the recruitment route."},{"type":"table","header":["PG route","Best for"],"rows":[[{"text":"M.Tech Aerospace Engineering"},{"text":"General aerospace R&D"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Aerodynamics/CFD"},{"text":"Aerodynamics"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Propulsion"},{"text":"Engines/rockets"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Aerospace Structures"},{"text":"Structural engineering"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Flight Dynamics & Control"},{"text":"GNC"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Avionics"},{"text":"Aerospace electronics"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Space Engineering"},{"text":"Spacecraft"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Mechanical Engineering"},{"text":"Broad aerospace engineering"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Materials"},{